{
  "abstract": "A smooth full-dimensional lattice polytope of positive dimension n whose edges have lattice length at least n has the integer decomposition property, and over every field its homogeneous toric ideal is generated by equal-sum quadratic binomials. For smooth polytopes with the same normal fan, edge bound n gives prescribed-parity decompositions of interior lattice points of their Minkowski sum. Edge bound n+1 gives the adjoint Minkowski equality. The latter two are the polytope formulations of Theorems 1.2 and 1.3.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Caius Folkerts"
    }
  ],
